Not long after the move, the Roman Empire's western provinces, including Rome, fell to the barbarians.

201
00:15:08,921 --> 00:15:17,920
In 330 AD, the Roman Empire, with Constantinople as its capital, became known as the Eastern Roman Empire, later called the Byzantine Empire.

202
00:15:17,921 --> 00:15:24,920
Constantine's decision to relocate had changed the course of history, making Constantinople the most powerful place on earth.

