Today, Ia Sophia is the only building of the three still standing

207
00:15:40,181 --> 00:15:46,860
above the ground. The original Hippodrome was built in 203 AD

208
00:15:46,861 --> 00:15:50,760
by the Roman Emperor Septimus Severus, but in 324 AD

209
00:15:50,761 --> 00:15:54,860
Emperor Constantine began to add his own land by expanding the original

210
00:15:54,861 --> 00:15:57,920
structure to rival Circus Maximus in Rome.

211
00:15:57,921 --> 00:16:00,980
He added more seats, enough to fit 100,000

212
00:16:00,981 --> 00:16:06,700
cheering spectators, and extended the U-shaped track to over 1,300 feet long and approximately

213
00:16:06,701 --> 00:16:11,602
250 feet wide, an arena the size of five and a half football fields.

214
00:16:11,603 --> 00:16:13,260
He decorated the center

215
00:16:13,261 --> 00:16:18,282
spina, or medium, with monuments brought in from regions throughout the empire.

216
00:16:18,283 --> 00:16:18,983
These

217
00:16:18,984 --> 00:16:23,360
monuments were a reflection of Rome's power, but were also used to block the view of the

