439
00:28:43,281 --> 00:28:44,720
on Modern Marvels.

440
00:28:55,340 --> 00:28:57,480
Today we know this city as Istanbul,

441
00:28:57,920 --> 00:28:59,540
but almost 1,700 years ago,

442
00:28:59,541 --> 00:29:04,680
this was Constantinople, the very spot that Emperor Constantine handpicked to be the new

443
00:29:04,681 --> 00:29:06,264
capital of the Roman Empire.

444
00:29:06,265 --> 00:29:09,940
Constantine wanted his capital to be bigger and better than Rome.

445
00:29:10,640 --> 00:29:14,899
He started by building a palace that would become the envy of the world.

446
00:29:14,900 --> 00:29:16,200
So where is this grand

447
00:29:16,201 --> 00:29:17,013
palace now?

448
00:29:17,014 --> 00:29:22,700
The palatial complex Constantine built here when he relocated his capital was

449
00:29:22,701 --> 00:29:28,480
called the Great Palace and stretched for approximately 860,000 square feet.

450
00:29:29,240 --> 00:29:31,620
That's larger than 15 football fields.

451
00:29:32,280 --> 00:29:36,680
The palace compound began at the Sea of Marmara and continued all the way to the Hippodrome.

452
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:41,340
Off limits to the public, it was like a small city for the emperor and his royal court.

453
00:29:42,120 --> 00:29:47,660
The grounds housed state buildings, throne rooms, churches, libraries, thermal baths,

454
00:29:47,661 --> 00:29:49,820
fountains, and ornate courtyards.

455
00:29:49,821 --> 00:29:57,600
Its bronze gates, roaring mechanical lions, and mosaic tile sidewalks made it one of the wonders of the ancient world.

456
00:30:00,920 --> 00:30:09,320
But towards the end of the Byzantine Empire, in a much debated move, the royal family left this grandeur for a smaller palace further inland.

457
00:30:09,860 --> 00:30:16,580
No one is exactly sure why, but this decision was the start of the decline of Constantine's famous great palace.

458
00:30:16,581 --> 00:30:21,860
When the Fourth Crusade sacked the city in 1204, the Crusaders are said to have lived

459
00:30:21,861 --> 00:30:25,900
in the remains of the palace they helped to destroy, and even stored their stolen loot

460
00:30:25,901 --> 00:30:26,900
there.

461
00:30:26,901 --> 00:30:32,640
The Ottomans conquered in 1453 and began to rebuild the area to suit their needs, recycling

462
00:30:32,641 --> 00:30:34,700
materials left behind.

463
00:30:34,701 --> 00:30:39,540
Soon, walls of the palace became walls of Ottoman homes.

464
00:30:39,541 --> 00:30:42,580
Byzantine stones helped build new mosques.

465
00:30:42,581 --> 00:30:47,160
After 470 years of Ottoman rule, the great palace slowly had disappeared beneath the

466
00:30:47,161 --> 00:30:50,400
ground and was all but forgotten.

